-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hearth is built on open-source packages installed from npm and listed in
package.json and package-lock.json, each under its own licence (MIT, ISC,
Apache-2.0 or similar). The main ones are:

- React and React DOM (MIT) - Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates
- React Router (MIT) - Remix Software Inc.
- TanStack Query (MIT) - Tanner Linsley
- Radix UI primitives (MIT) - WorkOS
- UI components in src/components/ui/ derived from shadcn/ui (MIT) - shadcn
- Tailwind CSS and tailwindcss-animate (MIT)
- Lucide icons, lucide-react (ISC) - Lucide Contributors
- Recharts (MIT), date-fns (MIT), Zod (MIT), React Hook Form (MIT),
  Sonner (MIT), cmdk (MIT), Vaul (MIT)
- Express (MIT) - OpenJS Foundation and contributors
- node-postgres, pg (MIT) - Brian Carlson
- Vite and TypeScript (build tools; MIT and Apache-2.0)

The licence text of each package is in its directory under node_modules/ after
`npm ci`, and is included in the built web app where the package requires it.

The Docker image is built on the official node image, and docker-compose.yml
uses the official postgres image; each is subject to its own licences.
